<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shizhaishan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shizhaishan is a low hill near Jinning, by the southern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-dian">Lake Dian</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, site of a royal cemetery of the Dian kingdom. Excavations from 1955 uncovered tombs rich in bronze drums, weapons and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cowrie-shell">cowrie</a> containers topped with lively scenes of figures. In 1956 a gold seal inscribed 'Seal of the King of Dian' was found there, matching the grant by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu of Han</a> recorded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-qian">Sima Qian</a>.</p></div>
